# data/raw/ is deliberately NOT ignored: raw SERP responses are archival
# evidence, and CLAUDE.md's position is that historical PAA data is the asset
# nobody else has.
#
# Location dumps are the exception. They come from a FREE endpoint, are
# reproducible at any time, and locations-US.json alone is ~15 MB. They stay on
# disk as a local cache but do not belong in the repository.
data/raw/locations-*.json

# Screenshots of dashboards. Kept out of the repository on purpose: a Railway
# or DataForSEO panel screenshot shows live environment variables - API
# passwords, the database URL with its password, the callback token - in
# plain text. `git add -A` would sweep one straight into a commit, and a
# secret in git history outlives the file it arrived in.
#
# Look at them locally, then delete them. Do not commit them.
Ekran görüntüsü*.png
Ekran goruntusu*.png
Screenshot*.png
screenshot*.png
